   "id": "camps",
   "title": "The Sultan's army reaches the walls",
   "time": "2-5 April 1453",
   "narrative": "Mehmed II brings an army that Western sources put in the tens of thousands up to the Theodosian land walls, the one side of the city not guarded by water. The camp is pitched on Monday 2 April. His red-and-gold tent stands near the Mesoteichion, the middle stretch where the little river Lycus passes under the wall, and the guns and the elite Janissaries are placed around it. European regulars under Karaca Pasha stretch along the northern wall, Anatolian regulars under Ishak Pasha hold the southern stretch, and irregular bashi-bazouks wait behind. Zagan Pasha takes troops north of the Golden Horn. In the sea, Baltoghlu's fleet gathers.",
