   "id": "defenders",
   "title": "The defenders take their posts",
   "time": "5 April 1453",
   "narrative": "With about eight thousand fighting men for roughly twenty kilometres of walls, the defenders can only man the outer land wall. Emperor Constantine XI and his Greeks hold the Mesoteichion, the section feared most. Giovanni Giustiniani and his Genoese stand north of him at the Charisian Gate and later join the emperor at the centre. The Venetians under Minotto hold the Blachernae palace corner, while Theophilos Palaiologos, Filippo Contarini and Demetrios Kantakouzenos watch the southern gates. Reserves are kept back in the Petra quarter, and Alviso Diedo commands the ships inside the Golden Horn behind the chain.",
