   "id": "bombardment",
   "title": "The great guns open fire",
   "time": "6 April - mid April",
   "narrative": "The bombardment begins. Orban's giant gun, hauled from Edirne by a team of oxen and hundreds of men, and other bombards batter the wall around the Mesoteichion. They fire slowly and imprecisely, and each night the defenders mend the damage with timber, earth and barrels. Mehmed also sends detachments to take outlying strongholds such as Therapia and Studius. Janissary rushes against the wall cost many lives, as the Venetian surgeon Barbaro recorded, because the Turks would not leave their dead behind.",
