  {
   "id": "four-ships",
   "title": "Four ships break the blockade",
   "time": "20 April 1453",
   "narrative": "Baltoghlu's fleet cannot force the chain across the mouth of the Golden Horn. On 20 April a small flotilla of Christian ships, running before a wind, fights its way through the Ottoman galleys and reaches the harbour. The success cheers the defenders and humiliates the Sultan; Baltoghlu, probably wounded in the eye, is stripped of his property and whipped. The relief also shows that Western help had not arrived in force.",
