  {
   "id": "fireships",
   "title": "The fireship attack fails",
   "time": "28 April 1453",
   "narrative": "On the night of 28 April the defenders try to burn the Ottoman ships now in the Golden Horn. The attempt fails, and many of the Italian crews are lost. Forty swimmers who reach the northern shore are impaled in view of the city; in reprisal the defenders execute 260 Ottoman prisoners on the walls. The failure leaves the defenders stretched, with part of their small force committed to the sea walls.",
