   "id": "mines",
   "title": "Mines and countermines",
   "time": "16-25 May 1453",
   "narrative": "Mehmed turns to the earth. Serbian miners from Novo Brdo, under Zagan Pasha, dig tunnels toward the walls. The German engineer Johannes Grant, serving with the Genoese, runs countermines, and the defenders break into the Ottoman galleries, kill the miners and use Greek fire. Tunnels are cut off on 16, 21, 23 and 25 May. Two captured Turkish officers on 23 May reveal where the rest run, and those are destroyed.",
