  {
   "id": "council",
   "title": "An offer refused, a council held",
   "time": "21-27 May 1453",
   "narrative": "On 21 May Mehmed offers to lift the siege if the city is handed over: the emperor would keep life and goods and rule the Peloponnese. Constantine will pay more tribute but will not give up the city. Halil Pasha urges the Sultan to withdraw, while Zagan Pasha demands an all-out assault, and Mehmed chooses the assault. On 27 May a Venetian scouting squadron reaches the city and reports that no relief fleet is coming. By then the guns have fired about 5,000 shots.",
