   "title": "The wall is lost",
   "time": "c. 05:00-08:00, 29 May",
   "narrative": "Janissaries led by Ulubatli Hasan pour over the wall and through the gaps, and the defence collapses at several points. Many Greeks run home to protect their families, the Venetians seek their ships, and a few Genoese flee to Galata. Constantine is last seen leading a final charge; sources differ and his fate is unknown. The Catalans on their stretch of wall are the last to fall. An Ottoman force reaches the Golden Horn walls from behind, and the Venetians break open a harbour gate to escape.",
