   "id": "sack",
   "title": "The city is taken",
   "time": "29 May 1453 (midday onward)",
   "narrative": "The Ottoman army spreads along the Mese, the main avenue, past the great forums toward the Church of the Holy Apostles, while the navy takes control of the Golden Horn by midday. A few Venetian and Genoese ships escape with refugees. The crowds sheltering in Hagia Sophia are taken when the doors are broken, and the captives are sorted by value for the slave markets. Thousands die; sources count about 4,000 Greek civilians killed and some 30,000 enslaved. The Byzantine Empire is over.",
